Section 1 Welcome depth layering and heading changes are landed and ready for coordinator verification.

The Welcome scene now assigns distinct depth layers (far, mid, near) with corresponding scale, pace, z-index, and blur values, and triggers periodic heading turns on `nextTurn`. A full Playwright behavior test suite verifies circularity, speed and depth separation, heading turns, replay stability, and still-mode positioning.

### What now works
1. Depth layers (far, mid, near) are assigned to Welcome scene bubbles in [`welcome.js`](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-welcome/public/color-polish/scenes/welcome.js) with scale factors (0.84, 0.93, 1.0), blur caps (0.9px, 0.35px, 0px), pace multipliers (0.7, 0.9, 1.15), and z-index offsets (40, 60, 80).
2. Seeded heading changes rotate velocity vectors by 25 to 70 degrees when `V.clock >= a.nextTurn`, rescheduling turns every 4 to 10 seconds.
3. Bubbles stay circular through all motion, resize, and replay cycles.
4. In reduced motion (still mode), transform translation is bypassed so slots remain at their initial inline coordinates.
5. All five behavior test scenarios are implemented in [`welcome.spec.ts`](file:///Users/anthony/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-welcome/tests/color-polish-scenes/welcome.spec.ts).

